STEP 2 -- create the two triggers (designed by the tester)                PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: build two triggers on the same port, one for `down` and one for `up`, so that
  each event can tell them apart.  One `shutdown` must fire trigger 1 and only trigger 1.
  One `no shutdown` must fire trigger 2 and only trigger 2.  `type` is sent before
  `description`, because the DUT refuses a description before a type.
  Expected: both are accepted, appear in `show trigger`, and start at zero activations.

awplus# configure terminal
awplus(config)# trigger 1
awplus(config-trigger)# type interface port1.0.2 down
awplus(config-trigger)# description ck down on port1.0.2
awplus(config-trigger)# trap
awplus(config-trigger)# repeat forever
awplus(config-trigger)# exit
awplus(config)# trigger 2
awplus(config-trigger)# type interface port1.0.2 up
awplus(config-trigger)# description ck up on port1.0.2
awplus(config-trigger)# trap
awplus(config-trigger)# repeat forever
awplus(config-trigger)# end

