  A note for whoever reads a running-config next.
  `show running-config | include trigger` prints only:
    trigger 1
    trigger 2
  The sub-mode lines (`type interface port1.0.2 down`, `description ...`, `trap`,
  `repeat forever`) do not contain the word "trigger", so the filter drops them.  That
  grep tells you a trigger EXISTS and nothing about what it does.  `show trigger <n>` is
  the command that does.  Do not read the short output as "the sub-commands were lost".
  => STEP 2 PASS: both triggers were created type-first, are Active with Trap Yes, and
     start from zero activations.

