STEP 6 -- the action: the trigger runs its script list (tester design)    PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: a trigger's action is a script from its list of 5.  No `.scp` file exists on
  this DUT's flash and none can be put there from this seat.  But the ATTEMPT is
  observable.  A reference to a file that does not exist is accepted and stored, so a
  deliberately absent file turns "did the trigger run its action?" into a question the
  DUT's own log answers.  Trigger 1 was re-armed; trigger 2 was deliberately left
  inactive, so the following up event is also a control.
  Expected: trigger 1 activates again, the DUT logs the activation, and the DUT logs its
  attempt to open the script file.

awplus(config)# trigger 1
awplus(config-trigger)# active
awplus(config-trigger)# script 1 flash:/cktrig.scp
  % Script /flash/cktrig.scp does not exist. Please ensure it is created before the
    trigger is activated
awplus(config-trigger)# end
awplus# show trigger 1
  Active ...................... Yes
  Number of activations ....... 1
  Number of scripts ........... 1
    1. flash:/cktrig.scp
    2. <not configured>
                                     <-- the reference IS stored, although the file is
                                         absent

box$ tools/tb capture tb277 ckmgmt eth3 110 t33416-script.pcap udp port 162
awplus(config)# interface port1.0.2 / shutdown / end   ... then ... no shutdown

  Trigger ..................... 1
  Number of activations ....... 2                            <-- fired again
  Last activation ............. Mon Oct 19 23:26:46 2026
  Trigger ..................... 2
  Number of activations ....... 1
  Last activation ............. Mon Oct 19 23:20:47 2026     <-- UNCHANGED: still inactive

  The DUT's own log, verbatim, which is the evidence for this step:

  2026 Oct 19 23:26:05 user.warning awplus IMI[903]: Script /flash/cktrig.scp does not
    exist. Please ensure it is created before the trigger is activated
